The Administration will be responsible for the following matters:
1. planning, promotion, and implementation of policies for health promotion, reablement, community support, and other welfare services regarding long-term care, senior citizens, and people with physical and mental disabilities, as well as enactment of relevant regulations;
2. planning, promotion, and implementation of resources for health promotion, reablement, community support, and other welfare services regarding long-term care, senior citizens, and people with physical and mental disabilities, as well as enactment of relevant regulations;
3. planning, promotion, and implementation of matters concerning the protection of the rights, maintenance of safety, and social participation in relation to long-term care, senior citizens, and people with physical and mental disabilities;
4. promotion, coordination, and liaison for the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities;
5. drafting, promotion, and implementation of laws and regulations concerning social welfare foundations and institutional long-term care juridical entities;
6. establishment, modification, revocation, annulment, supervision, guidance, and financial auditing of social welfare charitable trusts, as well as the drafting, promotion, and implementation of related laws and regulations;
7. supervision, guidance, and evaluation of the operations of long-term care, senior citizen, and disability service institutions;
8. planning, promotion, and implementation of the national pension program, as well as enactment of relevant regulations;
9. development of Information and Communications Technology (ICT) applications, international cooperation, and engagement regarding long-term care, senior citizens, people with physical and mental disabilities and national pension operations;
10. supervision, guidance, and evaluation of welfare service matters concerning long-term care, senior citizens, and people with physical and mental disabilities;
11. other matters related to welfare and rights services for long-term care, senior citizens, and people with physical and mental disabilities, and to national pension affairs.
